  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district. Governmental figures from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5; row labels on p4, amounts on p5). The Nutrition Fund is the only business-type fund (p7). The p4/p5 statement prints a Transfer from General Fund (2,034,806) and a matching Transfer to Activity Fund, both eliminated in the total column, so transfers_in/out are null. Bond proceeds 12,000,000 (Building Fund) are in the printed total receipts, so debt_proceeds is set and reported_totals includes debt_proceeds; governmental receipt items therefore sum to 93,311,942. Beginning/ending cash are fund balances (cash plus county treasurer cash); ending ties to the balance sheet p3 (42,363,836 cash + 11,959,840 county treasurer). Balance sheet (re-check 2026-10-28, attempt 2): governmental lines now from the Balance Sheet - Governmental Funds - Modified Cash Basis (p3, Total Governmental Funds: assets 54,323,676, no liabilities, equal to the government-wide Governmental Activities on p1), with fund balance by classification (Restricted 27,912,152 in 4 lines; Assigned 48,081 + 3,245,244 + 10,970,476; Unassigned 12,147,723); the business-type cash and unrestricted net position 1,768,199 and the printed totals stay from the Statement of Net Position (p1, Total column). Statement 'State aid and grants' already excludes homestead, property tax credit and pro-rate (printed as their own lines). 'Fines and licenses' 528,091 mixes county fines and license fees, local license fees and police court fines (review). Labels corrected to as printed (Sale of property, Special education, Interest income). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p8) has function-level spending only (no object breakdown); sale of property is inside printed total receipts so recorded as revenue; GF Transfer to Activity Fund shown as other financing (negative) and the expenditure total includes it. Building and QCPU revenue totals include loan/bond proceeds (other financing). GF schedule donations (50+82,384) plus community service 25,968 total 108,402, equal to statement donations 79,434 + other income 28,968 (3,000 classified differently). Business-type: measure cash (modified cash basis; net position equals cash 1,768,199); lunch sales charges; state sources state aid; federal sources and USDA commodities federal grants; nonoperating interest income included in receipts; no single printed total, so business-type receipts total is operating 3,995,092 + 8,721. Combining schedule p12 recorded per fund (Employee Benefit fund had no activity). Read pages 1-12 of 12."
